--- a/docs/change_log/release-3.4.md
+++ b/docs/change_log/release-3.4.md
@@ -58,6 +58,20 @@ In addition, the `md_globals` parameter of
 `Markdown.extensions.Extension.extendMarkdown()` is no longer recognized as a
 valid parameter and will raise an error if provided.
 
+### The `UnescapePostprocessor` has been deprecated in favor of the new `UnescapeTreeprocessor`.
+
+Backslash escaped characters used to be restored by the `UnescapePostprocessor` *after* the
+document had been serialized, which meant that the restored characters never got HTML escaped.
+A backslash escaped character which has special meaning in HTML (for example, a `"` when using
+the [smarty](../extensions/smarty.md) extension) could therefore produce invalid HTML when used
+in an attribute value, such as the `alt` text of an image.
+
+The new `UnescapeTreeprocessor` restores backslash escaped characters in the ElementTree before
+it is serialized, so the serializer escapes them properly. As a result, some characters may now
+be output as HTML entities (for example, `\>` now results in `&gt;` instead of `>`). The
+`UnescapePostprocessor` is no longer registered by default and will be removed in a future
+release; it raises a `DeprecationWarning` when used.
+
 ## New features
 
 The following new features have been included in the 3.4 release:
